Type: Package
Package: aelectoral2
Title: Processing, Analysis and Visualization of Mexican Electoral Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Rafael", "Lopez", email = "rlopez@morant.com.mx",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Emilio", "Morones", role = "aut"),
    person("Déborah", "Martínez", role = "aut"),
    person("Pablo", "Morales", role = "aut"),
    person("Morant Consultores", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: An object-oriented (R6) framework to process, analyze and
    visualize Mexican electoral data at multiple geographic levels
    (sections, municipalities and districts). It handles coalition vote
    splitting, special and foreign votes, winner and relative-result
    calculations, electoral "rentabilidad" (profitability) modelling, and
    high-level cartographic and statistical visualizations. Large
    electoral, shapefile and census resources are loaded through a hybrid
    local-first / cached / remote (Google Drive) strategy to keep the
    installed package lightweight.
URL: https://github.com/morant-consultores/aelectoral2
BugReports: https://github.com/morant-consultores/aelectoral2/issues
